        "title": "Competitive Flexible Procedure (CFP)  Aldbanks Supported Living  CBC-2074-CFP-SK",
        "description": "Central Bedfordshire Council is seeking to appoint a suitably experienced provider to deliver supported living services at Aldbanks. The service will provide high-quality, person-centred support to adults with eligible care and support needs, enabling individuals to maximise their independence, maintain their wellbeing, and participate fully in their local community. The successful provider will work collaboratively with the Council, residents, families, health partners and other stakeholders to deliver safe, effective and outcome-focused support that promotes choice, control and independence.\nThis procurement is being conducted as a two-stage Competitive Flexible Procedure under the Procurement Act 2023. At this first stage, Suppliers are required to complete the Participation and Selection Questionnaire. Following evaluation, the four highest-scoring qualified Suppliers will be invited to participate in Stage 2 and submit a full Tender Response.\nThe Council will provide as much support and information as it can to help guide Suppliers through the tender process. Questions raised by Suppliers, together with the Council's responses, will be shared with all Suppliers through the Procurement Portal to ensure a fair and transparent process.\nIf there is anything you are unsure about or require clarification on, please use the Correspondence facility within the In-Tend electronic tendering system.\nDeadline for submission of clarification questions: Monday 26 October 2026.\nCompleted Participation and Selection Questionnaire responses and supporting attachments must be submitted electronically via the In-Tend system. Responses must be uploaded through the \"My Return\" section of the system. Responses submitted through the Correspondence facility will not be considered.\nDeadline for submission of completed Participation and Selection Questionnaire responses: Monday 2 November 2026 at 12:00 noon.",
